~ start
Cake: Hey. Careful with the candles, I am trying to look majestic.
Lena: ...Did the cake just talk?
Cake: Of course. This is a birthday project. Standards are higher here.
- Are you really the final cake?
	Lena: Are you really the final cake?
	Cake: Final? I prefer "legendary". But yes, I am the cake at the end of the room.
	Cake: I waited in dramatic lighting for this exact conversation.
	=> wish
- You sound very confident for a dessert.
	Lena: You sound very confident for a dessert.
	Cake: Confidence is just sugar with posture.
	Cake: Also, I have three layers and a mission.
	=> wish
- I only came here to stare respectfully.
	Lena: I only came here to stare respectfully.
	Cake: Respect accepted. You may also admire the frosting from a safer distance.
	=> END

~ wish
Cake: Since you made it this far, you are allowed one ceremonial birthday thought.
- Then I wish Lena a very happy birthday.
	Lena: Then I wish Lena a very happy birthday.
	Cake: Excellent choice. Warm, correct, no notes.
	Cake: Let the room remember this moment.
	=> END
- Then I wish for a huge slice of cake.
	Lena: Then I wish for a huge slice of cake.
	Cake: Brave. Slightly threatening, but brave.
	Cake: I respect the honesty.
	=> END
- Then I wish this place stays a little magical.
	Lena: Then I wish this place stays a little magical.
	Cake: That one is already working, but it helps to say it out loud.
	=> END
